title: A 'cost-state' record is the cost of one run of the process, so it is not a session's total.
pid: d9f4ae45-70a3-4896-a5ea-7dfa9254c79f
body: |2-
  It starts again from nothing when a session is resumed: Jeff's
  session 'Top' (4fc4ae11, two days, resumed) has a last 'cost-state'
  of a fraction of what its records sum to. A process killed before it
  writes one leaves none (4c5f34ac, cut off by a container stop). Use
  it to check prices, not to total.
